course: dictionary
lesson: 10785
title: A grand old word: valour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Valour means great courage, the kind shown when facing battle or danger. It is a grand old word, and you will meet it in stories about knights and heroes. «Won back by matchless valour, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» The clues are won back and a fight, so valour must mean bravery.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in: «Won back by matchless bravery, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Matchless and consummate are big, grand words too, and they show the author is praising the animals.
explain: Valour is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say great valour, not a valour. In American English it is spelled valor.
fact: Valour means great courage, especially in battle or danger.
fact: On the Victoria Cross medal, the words «For Valour» are written to honour brave deeds.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the animals fight bravely to win back Toad Hall, and Toad boasts of his valour afterwards.
fact: «Acts of valour» are brave deeds done in the face of danger.
fact: Shakespeare's Falstaff says «discretion is the better part of valour», which means it is wiser to be careful than to be brave in a foolish way.
exercise: «Won back by matchless valour, consummate strategy, and a proper handling of sticks.» What does valour mean here? | *Great courage in battle or danger | A sunny day at the seaside | Fancy clothes for a party | Hunger and tiredness
exercise: The medal says «For Valour». What is the medal honouring? | Good cooking | *Brave deeds in battle or danger | Winning a race | Calm, quiet thinking
exercise: Toad boasts of his valour. Which word means nearly the same as valour? | *Bravery | Sleepiness | Hunger | Cowardice
test: Falstaff says «discretion is the better part of valour». What does this mean? | Brave people never stop to think | *It is wiser to be careful than to be brave in a foolish way | Valour is a kind of food | Always fight first, whatever the danger
test: Valour is which part of speech? | Adjective | *Noun | Adverb | Verb
exam: Which spelling of valour is American? | *Valor | Valoure | Valur | Valour
